      "description": "Watch Dundee FC vs Aberdeen highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Scottish Premiership season continued with a high-stakes encounter as Dundee FC faced off against Aberdeen . Fans gathered in anticipation of a contest that promised both tactical discipline and offensive ambition from the opening whistle. Early Breakthrough and First Half Discipline On August 8, 2026 , the match ignited early with a showcase of clinical attacking play. In the 9th minute, the deadlock was broken when Joe Bevan turned provider, delivering a precise ball to Joe Westley , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. This early advantage for Aberdeen set the tone for a physical contest, as Dundee FC struggled to find an immediate rhythm. The intensity of the match was reflected in the referee's notebook, starting with a yellow card for Alexander Briedl in the 12th minute. As the first half progressed, the battle in midfield grew more contested. Lewis Mayo received a booking in the 38th minute for a mistimed challenge, and goalscorer Joe Westley joined him in the book just before the interval in the 44th minute. Despite the cautions, the visitors remained composed, maintaining their lead as both sides retreated to the dressing rooms for half-time adjustments. Bevan Doubles the Lead as Substitutions Flow The second half began with a tactical reshuffle, as Dundee FC introduced Lewis Smith and Ayoub Mouloua to inject energy into their lineup. However, it was Aberdeen who struck again to tighten their grip on the match. In the 56th minute, the roles shifted for Joe Bevan ; after assisting the opener, he found the net himself to double the lead. This second goal provided a significant cushion and forced the hosts into further defensive vulnerability as they chased the game. The final half-hour saw a flurry of activity on the benches, with both managers utilizing their full squads. Players like Finlay Robertson , Ashley Hay , and Jack Milne were introduced to manage the closing stages. Although Jack Milne picked up a late yellow card in the 90th minute, the result was never in doubt. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+4 minutes, confirming a disciplined and effective performance by the visitors on the road."
